@startuml 07-principals-two-places
!include theme-oriolrius.puml
title Principals: the two-places rule
left to right direction

rectangle "Alice's certificate\n(decided at issue time,\nfollows the person)" as cert <<user>> {
  rectangle "developers" as p1
  rectangle "u:alice" as p2
}
rectangle "Server web1: /etc/ssh/auth_principals/deploy\n(decided per host,\nfollows the server)" as file <<file>> {
  rectangle "developers\ndevelopers@web1.acme.example" as f1
}
rectangle "Login as deploy:\n**ALLOWED**" as ok <<host>>
p1 --> f1 : same label in both places
f1 --> ok
note bottom of ok
  Login allowed only if the certificate and auth_principals/<account> share at least one principal.
  In only one place: signature OK, but <color:#C62828>Permission denied (publickey)</color>
  sshd log: "Certificate does not contain an authorized principal"
end note
@enduml
